# The Global Top Bar

Across the top of the osionos shell sits a **VSCode-style chrome bar**, mounted
in `App.tsx` above the content. It is its own widget, `widgets/top-bar/`, and it
appears on both surfaces: the osionos editor and the opposite-osiris website.

## What's on the bar

Left to right:

1. **Logo**
2. **Menus** — `File · Edit · Selection · View · Help` (native Electron menu sync
   on the desktop build)
3. **Centre search / command bar** — page search by default; type `>` to switch
   to command mode
4. **Update button** — see [the Update/rebuild button](update-rebuild-button.xmd)
5. **Window controls** — minimise / maximise / close, **desktop only**

## Widget layout

The widget splits cleanly into model and UI:

| Layer | Files |
|:------|:------|
| `model/` | `desktop.ts` · `menus.ts` · `commands.ts` · `search.ts` · `usePalette.ts` |
| `ui/` | `TopBar` · `TopBarMenu` · `MenuDropdown` · `TopBarSearch` · `WindowControls` · `UpdateButton` |

Its own theme tokens — `--osio-topbar-{h,bg,border}` — were added to `global.css`,
so the bar restyles with the rest of the theme rather than carrying hard-coded
colours.

## Search that reaches your whole workspace

The centre bar started as a **client-side** search over the pages already loaded
in the store. That missed most real content: nested child pages are not all held
in the client cache, so search "only found Untitled".

It was moved server-side:

> [!success] Bridge-backed search
> The client calls a bridge endpoint that lists **all** workspace rows (title +
> content), ranked title-prefix → substring → content, scoped by owner/ACL. The
> input debounces the remote call and shows an instant local fallback plus a
> "Searching…" state while the network round-trips.

## Window controls only on desktop

`WindowControls` renders **only** when running inside the Electron desktop shell
(`isDesktop()`), where it calls the already-wired IPC bridge —
`window.osionosDesktop.{minimize, toggleMaximize, close}`. In the browser it
renders nothing.

> [!note] Keyboard chords
> The bar owns a set of global chords that don't collide with the editor's own
> `⌘B / ⌘I / ⌘U / ⌘E`: **`⌘K`** focuses search, **`⌘⇧P`** opens command mode, and
> **`⌘\`** splits the active pane. Command mode is detected **only** inside the
> top-bar input, so it never fights the in-document slash menu.

Continue → [The ⌘K command palette](command-palette.xmd).
